                <pb facs="0917" n="803" xml:id="pg803"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/448: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-12T18:00:00-05:45">June 12, 1931—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 13—12:33 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>106. Department’s 111, May 9 [<hi rendition="#italic">8</hi>], 9 a.m. [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">5 p.m.</hi>] The Nicaragua-Honduras boundary protocol
                    has been under discussion for some days in the Nicaraguan Congress. The
                    opposition is active and strong in both political parties. President Moncada is
                    in Masaya giving the matter his personal attention and I understand that he is
                    still for approval.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
